PLUS the source's prohibition of military use (see below), which no standard license expresses.

Source and rights statements
- Source dataset: Andrzejak RG, Lehnertz K, Rieke C, Mormann F, David P, Elger CE. Indications of nonlinear
  deterministic and finite dimensional structures in time series of brain electrical activity: Dependence on
  recording region and brain state [dataset]. Repositori Digital de la UPF, 2001. doi:10.34810/data490,
  http://hdl.handle.net/10230/42894
- The repository record lists two rights statements (dc.rights), verbatim:
  1. "Licensed under a Creative Commons License (CC-BY) 4.0" (dc.rights.uri https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
  2. "The source codes, data and results on these sites are free of charge for research and education
     purposes only. Any commercial or military use is prohibited. All resources are provided without any
     expressed or implied warranty. In no event the authors of the article or any of their host institutions
     are liable for any damages arising from the use of the software, data or results."
  The UPF NTSA download page carries the same Legal Agreement (statement 2).

Why CC BY-NC 4.0: it is the closest standard license that honours both statements (attribution, and no
commercial use). Statement 2 also prohibits MILITARY use. That restriction is not expressible in a standard
Creative Commons license and applies in addition: use these data for research and education purposes only;
any commercial or military use is prohibited.

Attribution: cite Andrzejak RG, Lehnertz K, Mormann F, Rieke C, David P, Elger CE (2001) Phys. Rev. E 64,
061907, doi:10.1103/PhysRevE.64.061907, and doi:10.34810/data490.

Changes made: only the intracranial sets C, D, E are included (sets A and B, scalp EEG from healthy
volunteers, are omitted); format conversion only (ASCII integers to BrainVision INT_16, values identical);
BIDS metadata added. Original zip files of sets C, D, E are included unchanged in sourcedata/.
